# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Logs / scratch
*.log

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Machine-local Claude Code settings. `settings.local.json` is per-machine by
# convention (Claude Code merges it OVER settings.json and nothing ever writes it),
# which is the same reason /update tells a target to put personalizations there —
# so it must not be committed. Any SHARED setting for this repo belongs in a
# tracked .claude/settings.json instead.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code worktrees. `EnterWorktree` puts an isolated CHECKOUT OF THIS REPO at
# `.claude/worktrees/<name>/`, which git does not ignore on its own — so a `git add -A`
# in the main checkout stages an entire copy of the repo into itself. Caught by a
# `git status` showing a bare `?? .claude/` after the phase-9-capture worktree existed;
# nothing had committed it yet, and this is what stops the first one that would.
.claude/worktrees/

# The smoke-drive receipt: evidence that THIS working tree, at THIS commit, was driven
# end-to-end as an installed package. Machine-local on purpose and not committed — it names
# the HEAD it tested, so committing it would change the HEAD and invalidate itself on the way
# in. A clone has no receipt and must run its own drive, which is the correct answer: the
# receipt attests to a run that happened here, not to a claim that travels.
.smoke-receipt.json
